Syntax :-

upper_bound(f, l, val);
upper_bound(f, l, val, comp);

f: iterator to beginning of sequence
l: iterator to end of sequence
val: value whose upper bound needed to be found
comp: -- not clear yet --

What it returns ?

It returns the iterator to the first element in the given range
which is greater than val. If no such number exist returns iterator
one past the last element(by doing it - a.begin())

* upper_bound only works in sorted sequence
